{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 12: underachievement (limits to success). A sales force grows from the margin on shipments; orders outrun a fixed plant, delivery delay rises, and customers order less. }
Sales Reps= INTEG(
	Rep Hiring - Rep Departures,
	10)
	~	rep
	~	People selling the product.
	|
Reps per Unit Shipped=
	0.008
	~	rep/unit
	~	New reps funded by the margin on each unit shipped.
	|
Rep Hiring=
	Shipments * Reps per Unit Shipped
	~	rep/month
	~	|
Rep Tenure=
	24
	~	month
	~	Average time a rep stays.
	|
Rep Departures=
	Sales Reps / Rep Tenure
	~	rep/month
	~	|
Normal Orders per Rep=
	10
	~	unit/rep/month
	~	Orders a rep wins each month when delivery is normal.
	|
Delivery Elasticity=
	2
	~	dmnl
	~	How strongly customers react to a longer delivery delay than normal.
	|
Effect of Delivery Delay=
	(Normal Delivery Delay / Perceived Delivery Delay) ^ Delivery Elasticity
	~	dmnl
	~	1 at the normal delay, below 1 when delivery is slow.
	|
Order Rate=
	Sales Reps * Normal Orders per Rep * Effect of Delivery Delay
	~	unit/month
	~	|
Backlog= INTEG(
	Order Rate - Shipments,
	200)
	~	unit
	~	Orders accepted and not yet shipped.
	|
Normal Delivery Delay=
	2
	~	month
	~	Time to ship an order when the plant is not constrained.
	|
Shipments=
	MIN(Backlog / Normal Delivery Delay, Capacity)
	~	unit/month
	~	|
Delivery Delay=
	XIDZ(Backlog, Shipments, Normal Delivery Delay)
	~	month
	~	Months of backlog at the current shipment rate.
	|
Perception Time=
	3
	~	month
	~	Time for the market to notice a change in delivery delay.
	|
Perceived Delivery Delay=
	SMOOTH3(Delivery Delay, Perception Time)
	~	month
	~	|
Capacity= INTEG(
	Capacity Additions,
	400)
	~	unit/month
	~	Plant capacity.
	|
Expansion Switch=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	0: capacity is fixed (the problem). 1: capacity follows orders (the solution).
	|
Capacity Lead Time=
	6
	~	month
	~	Time to build capacity.
	|
Capacity Additions=
	Expansion Switch * MAX(0, Order Rate * Capacity Margin - Capacity) / Capacity Lead Time
	~	unit/month/month
	~	|
Capacity Margin=
	1.2
	~	dmnl
	~	Capacity planned above orders so that the plant is rarely the bottleneck.
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ month ~ |
FINAL TIME = 60 ~ month ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
